    "reliability of team halftime adjustment",
    "year-to-year correlation of H2-H1",
    "split-half reliability of defensive adjustment",
    "sample size requirements for team defensive traits",
    "confounding by game script and opposition",
    "measurement stability",
    "signal vs noise in halftime changes"
  ],
  "historical_evidence": [
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085",
      "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
      "finding": "Connector teammate-path quality Q_p had split-half reliability too low (Pearson r=0.215, Spearman-Brown 0.355) to treat as a stable scoutable trait; most variance is within-player half-to-half."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF18",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "Structural influence residual split-half stability was confirmed: pooled-residual rho=+0.685, usage-partial rho=+0.557, indicating a reproducible player property."
